fzy builds with -std=c99, which makes gcc define __STRICT_ANSI__. On illumos
that selects _STRICT_STDC in <sys/feature_tests.h>, which sets _STRICT_SYMBOLS
and hides fileno(), sigemptyset(), sigaddset() and strndup(). _GNU_SOURCE,
which fzy already sets, is a glibc macro with no effect here; __EXTENSIONS__ is
the illumos equivalent, and the only one that exposes everything needed --
_XOPEN_SOURCE=700 would re-hide the non-POSIX SIGWINCH and TIOCGWINSZ that
src/tty.c uses.

The test link rule compiles test/*.c directly but omits $(CPPFLAGS), so
preprocessor defines never reach the test sources. Upstream compensated with
per-file macros: "#define _GNU_SOURCE" in test/test_choices.c for asprintf()
and "#define _DEFAULT_SOURCE" in test/test_properties.c for strndup(). Routing
CPPFLAGS through the rule makes the feature macros uniform between src/ and
test/, so both per-file defines are removed -- the _GNU_SOURCE one would
otherwise clash with the command-line -D_GNU_SOURCE (empty vs 1) and warn
"_GNU_SOURCE redefined" on gcc and clang alike.

Identical to https://github.com/jhawthorn/fzy/pull/208, which should be dropped
from here if that lands.

--- a~/Makefile	2026-09-10 22:30:57.095621660 +0000
+++ a/Makefile	2026-09-10 22:30:57.098043283 +0000
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 VERSION=1.1
 
-CPPFLAGS=-DVERSION=\"${VERSION}\" -D_GNU_SOURCE
+CPPFLAGS=-DVERSION=\"${VERSION}\" -D_GNU_SOURCE -D__EXTENSIONS__
 CFLAGS+=-MD -Wall -Wextra -g -std=c99 -O3 -pedantic -Ideps -Werror=vla
 PREFIX?=/usr/local
 MANDIR?=$(PREFIX)/share/man
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ TESTOBJECTS=test/fzytest.c test/test_pro
 all: fzy
 
 test/fzytest: $(TESTOBJECTS)
-	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(CCFLAGS) -Isrc -o $@ $(TESTOBJECTS) $(LIBS)
+	$(CC) $(CPPFLAGS) $(CFLAGS) $(CCFLAGS) -Isrc -o $@ $(TESTOBJECTS) $(LIBS)
 
 acceptance: fzy
 	cd test/acceptance && bundle --quiet && bundle exec ruby acceptance_test.rb
